# threads are still building. The node_count is not synchronized.
# Thread 0 sees node_count=8124 but there are actually more nodes.
# The fix: after all threads complete building, we need to re-read node_count
# or use an atomic operation.
# Actually, the real issue is that node_count is a shared variable that
# threads increment concurrently. When a thread reads node_count to allocate
# the nodes array, it might see a stale value.
# Fix: use an atomic read or wait for all threads to finish before collecting.
# But all threads do the collection after building... 
